<title>FRANCE: RUGBY UNION-BOURGOIN WIN EUROPEAN CONFERENCE TITLE.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-BOURGOIN WIN EUROPEAN CONFERENCE TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>BEZIERS, France 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bourgoin beat Castres 18-9 (halftime 6-6) in the European Conference rugby union final on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Bourgoin - Penalties: Patrice Favre (3), Alexander Peclier (2). Drop-goal: Peclier.</p>
<p>Castres - Penalties: Cyril Savy (2), Sebastien Paillat.</p>
</text>
